{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 10962, "title": "why the index page keep generate static html on each request", "body": "add `page/index.js` to empty project, and includes these code:\r\n\r\n```\r\nexport default ({ number }) => {\r\n  console.log(\"index render\");\r\n  return (\r\n    <div>\r\n      <h1>Index : {number}</h1>\r\n    </div>\r\n  );\r\n};\r\n\r\nexport async function getStaticProps() {\r\n  console.log(\"index getStaticProps\");\r\n  return {\r\n    props: {\r\n      number: 1\r\n    }\r\n  };\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nthen I use `next build` command, it's print correctly in console.\r\n\r\n`next start` also work well\r\n\r\nbut when I request `http://localhost:3000/` in browser, the console log repeat every request except the first request.\r\n\r\ni check `.next` dir, the `index.html` generated correctly, but why the request trigger it generate again?\r\n\r\nbut when I copy the code to any other page, there is no problem, no console words out\r\n\r\ndid i miss something?", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 2, "reactions_total": 0, "reactions_plus": 0, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "yjisme", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2020-03-11T09:53:33Z", "updated_at": "2022-06-13T12:50:07Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/10962", "classification": "random"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 10964, "title": "How to use built-in css support?", "body": "I'm trying to remove next-css plugin in favor of built-in css support. So:\r\n\r\n - I removed `withCss` from my plugin list\r\n - I upgraded to next `9.3.0`\r\n\r\nBut whenever I attempt to import a global css file, (eg. `import 'foo.css'`) I get an error:\r\n\r\n> [ error ] ./src/test.css 1:0\r\nModule parse failed: Unexpected character '@' (1:0)\r\nYou may need an appropriate loader to handle this file type, currently no loaders are configured to process this file. See https://webpack.js.org/concepts#loaders", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 2, "reactions_total": 0, "reactions_plus": 0, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "warpdesign", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2020-03-11T10:00:56Z", "updated_at": "2023-03-12T02:36:18Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/10964", "classification": "random"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 10968, "title": "How to retrieve data from database in Editor of draft Js in next js?", "body": "\r\nI'm working with draftjs editor for post's content in next.js. And there is a page called postlist from where i can click against particular post for edit purpose. Now when i clicked on a particular post for edit it will redirect me to a new page where each details of the post retrieved from mongodb database. Now in the the page each details like post title, post subtitle, post slug, post featured image etc retrieved from database else description where i can edit each field. Now my post's content field is not retrieved from database in draftjs editor part. How to resolve this problem?\r\n\r\n\r\n---------------------------------\r\nThis Is My Code\r\n---------------------------------\r\n    import React, {useState, useEffect} from 'react'\r\n    import Router from 'next/router';\r\n    import {useSelector} from 'react-redux'\r\n    import DatePicker from 'react-datepicker';\r\n    import axios from 'axios';\r\n    import ImageSelector from './ImageSelector'\r\n    import  CheckBox  from './CheckBox'\r\n    import dynamic from 'next/dynamic'\r\n    import { EditorState, convertToRaw, ContentState } from 'draft-js';\r\n    import {stateToHTML} from 'draft-js-export-html'\r\n    import draftToHtml from 'draftjs-to-html';\r\n    import slug from 'limax';\r\n    // import htmlToDraft from 'html-to-draftjs';\r\n    let underscore;\r\n\r\n    const Editor = dynamic(() =>\r\n    import('react-draft-wysiwyg').then(mod => mod.Editor), {\r\n        ssr: false\r\n    })\r\n\r\n    const AddPost = (props) => {\r\n\r\n      const ref = React.createRef();\r\n      const [title, setTitle] = useState(props.post?props.post.title:'') \r\n      const [slugg, setSlug] = useState(props.post?props.post.slug:'')\r\n      const [hits,setHits] = useState(props.post?props.post.hits:'')\r\n      const [subtitle, setSubTitle] = useState(props.post?props.post.subtitle:'')\r\n      const [categoryname, setCategoryname] = useState(props.post?props.post.categoryname:'')\r\n      const [prevCategories, setprevCategoies] = useState(props.post?props.post.categoryname:'')\r\n      const [description, setDescription] = useState(props.post?props.post.description:'') \r\n      const [author, setAuthor] = useState(props.post?props.post.author:'')\r\n      const [location, setLocation] = useState(props.post?props.post.location:'')\r\n      const [date, setDate] = useState(new Date(props.post?props.post.date:new Date())) \r\n      const [actor, setActor] = useState(props.post?props.post.actor:[]) \r\n      const [id, setId] = useState() \r\n      const [imagepath, setImagepath] = useState(props.post?props.post.imagepath:'')\r\n      const [imagecaption, setImagecaption] = useState(props.post?props.post.imagecaption:'')\r\n      const [show, setShow] = useState(props.post?props.post.show:'')\r\n      const [categories, setCategories] = useState([]) \r\n      const [poststatus, setPoststatus] = useState(props.post?props.post.poststatus:'')\r\n      const [error, setError] = useState([])\r\n      const [editorState, setEditorState]= useState(EditorState.createEmpty()) \r\n      const [editorImages, setEditorImages] = useState([])\r\n\r\n      useEffect(() => {\r\n        dynamicImportFunc()\r\n        fetchCategories()\r\n      }, [])\r\n\r\n      const dynamicImportFunc = async () => {\r\n        if (typeof window !== 'undefined') {\r\n          const { default: htmlToDraft} = await import('html-to-draftjs')\r\n          // convertHtmlToDraft = htmlToDraft\r\n          if(props.post){\r\n            const contentBlock = htmlToDraft(props.post.description)\r\n            console.log(\"CONTENTBLOCK\", contentBlock)\r\n              if (contentBlock) {\r\n                const contentState = ContentState.createFromBlockArray(contentBlock.contentBlocks)\r\n                const editorState = EditorState.createWithContent(contentState)\r\n                console.log(editorState)\r\n\r\n                setEditorState(editorState)\r\n              }\r\n            }\r\n        }\r\n\r\n      }\r\n\r\n    //------------------------------------------------------------\r\n    // //--------------------------CATEGORY--------------------------\r\n    const fetchCategories = () => {\r\n      axios.get('http://localhost:5000/categories')\r\n      .then(response => {\r\n          let categories = []\r\n          response.data.forEach(cat => {\r\n            let category = {\r\n              _id: cat._id,\r\n              name: cat.categorytitle,\r\n              slug: cat.categoryslug,\r\n              parent: cat.parentCategory,\r\n              isChild: cat.isChild,\r\n              isChecked: prevCategories.includes(cat.categoryslug),\r\n              hasChildren: false\r\n            }\r\n            if(!cat.isChild){\r\n              let children = []\r\n              response.data.forEach(childCat => {\r\n                if(childCat.parentCategory && childCat.parentCategory === cat.categoryslug){\r\n                  children.push(childCat.categoryslug)\r\n                }\r\n              })\r\n              if(children.length > 0){\r\n                category.hasChildren = true\r\n                category = {...category, children: children}\r\n              }\r\n            }\r\n\r\n            categories.push(category)\r\n          })\r\n          setCategories(categories)\r\n      })\r\n      .catch((error) => {\r\n          console.log(error);\r\n      })\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    const handleAllChecked = (event) => {\r\n      let categoriess = categories\r\n      categoriess.forEach(category => category.isChecked = event.target.checked) \r\n      setCategories(categoriess) \r\n      console.log(categoriess)\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    const handleCheckChieldElement = (event) => {\r\n      let categoriess = categories \r\n      categoriess.forEach(category => {\r\n         if (category.name === event.target.value){\r\n            category.isChecked =  event.target.checked\r\n            console.log(category.name)\r\n            categories.forEach(parentCat => {\r\n              if(category.parent === parentCat.slug){\r\n                parentCat.isChecked = true\r\n              }\r\n            })\r\n          }\r\n      })\r\n      setCategories(categoriess) \r\n    }\r\n\r\n\r\n    //--------------------------------------------------\r\n    //-----------------POST DESCRIPTION-----------------\r\n\r\n      const onChangeTitle = (e) => {\r\n        setTitle(e.target.value) \r\n      }\r\n      const onChangeSubTitle = (e) => {\r\n        setSubTitle(e.target.value)\r\n      }\r\n\r\n\r\n      const onChangeDescription = (editorState) => {\r\n          setEditorState(editorState)\r\n      }\r\n\r\n      const embedCallback = (embeddedLink) => {\r\n        if (embeddedLink.indexOf(\"youtube\") >= 0){\r\n          embeddedLink = embeddedLink.replace(\"watch?v=\",\"embed/\");\r\n          embeddedLink = embeddedLink.replace(\"/watch/\", \"/embed/\");\r\n          embeddedLink = embeddedLink.replace(\"youtu.be/\",\"youtube.com/embed/\");\r\n        }\r\n        return embeddedLink\r\n      }\r\n\r\n      const uploadCallback = (file) => {\r\n        let uploadedImages = editorImages;\r\n\r\n        const formData = new FormData();\r\n        formData.append('file', file);\r\n\r\n        return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\r\n          axios.post('http://localhost:5000/Images/uploadImage', formData, {\r\n            headers: {\r\n              'Content-Type': 'multipart/form-data'\r\n            },\r\n          })\r\n          .then( res => {\r\n            console.log(res.data)\r\n            const imageObject = {\r\n              file: file,\r\n              localSrc: res.data,\r\n            }\r\n\r\n            uploadedImages.push(imageObject)\r\n\r\n            setEditorImages(uploadedImages) \r\n\r\n            resolve({ data: { link: res.data } });\r\n            console.log(res.data)\r\n          })\r\n          .catch(error => {\r\n              console.log(error)\r\n              reject(error.toString())\r\n          })\r\n\r\n        })   \r\n\r\n      }\r\n\r\n      const convertDescriptionFromJSONToHTML = () => {\r\n        try{\r\n          return { __html: stateToHTML(editorState.getCurrentContent())} \r\n        } catch(exp) {\r\n          console.log(exp)\r\n          return { __html: 'Error' }\r\n        }\r\n      }\r\n\r\n      const onChangeAuthor = (e) => {\r\n        setAuthor(e.target.value) \r\n      }\r\n      const onChangeLocation = (e) => {\r\n        setLocation(e.target.value)\r\n      }\r\n      const onChangeDate = (date) => {\r\n        setDate(date) \r\n      }\r\n      const onChangeSlug = (e) => {\r\n        setSlug(e.target.value)\r\n\r\n      }\r\n      const slugchange = (e) => {\r\n        e.preventDefault()\r\n        underscore = slug(title, '-')\r\n        setSlug(underscore) \r\n      }\r\n      const onSubmit = (e) => {\r\n        e.preventDefault()\r\n        savePost(false)\r\n      }\r\n\r\n      const savePost = (isDraft) => {\r\n\r\n        let descHTML =  draftToHtml(convertToRaw(editorState.getCurrentContent()))\r\n        if(\r\n          (title ==='') || (author ==='') \r\n          || (location ==='') || (date ==='') \r\n          || (imagepath ==='') || (categoryname ===[]) \r\n          || (slugg ==='')\r\n        )\r\n        {\r\n          alert('Please fill the fileds')\r\n          return false\r\n        }\r\n        let selectcatg = []\r\n        categories.forEach(catg => {\r\n          if(catg.isChecked) \r\n            selectcatg.push(catg.slug)\r\n        })\r\n        const post = {\r\n          title: title,\r\n          subtitle: subtitle,\r\n          description: descHTML,\r\n          author: author,\r\n          location: location,\r\n          date: date,\r\n          imagepath: imagepath,\r\n          imagecaption:imagecaption,\r\n          categoryname: selectcatg,\r\n          slug: slugg,\r\n          hits: hits,\r\n          poststatus: isDraft ? 'draft' : 'published'\r\n        }\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n        if(props.post){\r\n          axios.put('http://localhost:5000/posts/'+id,  post)   \r\n          .then(res => {\r\n            console.log(res.data)\r\n            alert('Post Updated Successfully')\r\n            setPoststatus('Published')\r\n          })\r\n          .catch(err => console.log(err))\r\n        }\r\n        else{\r\n          axios.post('http://localhost:5000/posts/addpost/', post)\r\n          .then(  res => {\r\n            console.log(\"RUNNING\")\r\n            if(res.status !== 200){\r\n              console.log(res.status)\r\n              return\r\n            }\r\n            alert('Post saved Successfully')\r\n            setPoststatus('Draft')\r\n          })\r\n          .catch(error => {\r\n            console.log(\"ERROR:\",error)\r\n          })\r\n        }\r\n\r\n\r\n      }\r\n\r\n    const showModal = () => {\r\n      setShow(true)\r\n    };\r\n\r\n    const hideModal = () => {\r\n      setShow(false)\r\n    };\r\n\r\n      const setFeaturedImage = (path, caption) => {\r\n        setImagepath(path)\r\n        setImagecaption(caption)\r\n      }\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n        return (\r\n            <div style={{width:'100%',overflow:'hidden'}}>\r\n              <div style={{width:'100%',height:50,backgroundColor:'#1abc9c', color:'#ffffff',textAlign:'left'}}>\r\n                <h1 style={{marginLeft:150,textShadow:'5px 5px 5px #5a5a5a'}}>Add Post Here</h1>\r\n              </div>\r\n              <div className=\"addpost\" >\r\n                      <form noValidate onSubmit={onSubmit} className=\"formadd\">\r\n                          <div className=\"firstcolumn\">\r\n                            <div className=\"titleslug\">\r\n                              <div className=\"title\">\r\n                                  <input type=\"text\"\r\n                                  className=\"title\"\r\n                                  placeholder=\"Enter Title\"\r\n                                  value={title}\r\n                                  onChange={onChangeTitle}/>\r\n                              </div>\r\n                              <button className=\"slugbutton\" onClick={slugchange}>Generate Slug</button><br/><br/>\r\n                            </div><br/>\r\n                            <div className=\"slug-group\">\r\n                                <input type=\"text\"\r\n                                className=\"slug\"\r\n                                name=\"slug\"\r\n                                onClick={slugchange}\r\n                                ref={ref}\r\n                                placeholder=\"Enter Slug\"\r\n                                value={slugg}\r\n                                onChange={onChangeSlug}/>\r\n                            </div>\r\n                            <br/>\r\n                            <div className=\"form-group\">\r\n                                <input type=\"text\"\r\n                                className=\"subtitle\"\r\n                                placeholder=\"Enter Subtitle\"\r\n                                value={subtitle}\r\n                                onChange={onChangeSubTitle}/>\r\n                            </div><br/>\r\n                            <div>\r\n                            <input style={{height:'300px'}} type=\"text\"\r\n                                className=\"subtitle\"\r\n                                placeholder=\"Enter Subtitle\"\r\n                                value={editorState}\r\n                                onChange={onChangeDescription}/>\r\n                              <Editor\r\n                                initialEditorState={editorState}\r\n                                wrapperClassName=\"wrapper-class\"\r\n                                editorClassName=\"editor-class\"\r\n                                toolbarClassName=\"toolbar-class\"\r\n                                wrapperStyle={{ }}\r\n                                editorStyle={{ height: \"300px\", padding: \"10px\"}}\r\n                                // toolbarStyle={<toolbarStyleObject>}\r\n                                onEditorStateChange={onChangeDescription}\r\n                                toolbar={{ \r\n                                  image: { uploadCallback: uploadCallback, previewImage: true },\r\n                                  embedded: { embedCallback: embedCallback }\r\n                                }}\r\n                              />\r\n                            </div><br/>\r\n\r\n                            <div className=\"authorloction\">\r\n                              <div className=\"author\">\r\n                                  <label htmlFor=\"author\">Author:</label>\r\n                                  <input type=\"text\"\r\n                                  className=\"author\"\r\n                                  name=\"author\"\r\n                                  placeholder=\"Enter Author Name\"\r\n                                  value={author}\r\n                                  onChange={onChangeAuthor}/>\r\n                              </div>\r\n                              <div className=\"location\">\r\n                                  <label htmlFor=\"location\">Location:</label>\r\n                                  <input type=\"text\"\r\n                                  className=\"location\"\r\n                                  name=\"location\"\r\n                                  placeholder=\"Enter Location\"\r\n                                  value={location}\r\n                                  onChange={onChangeLocation}/>\r\n                              </div>\r\n                            </div>\r\n                          </div>\r\n                          <div className=\"secondcolumn\">\r\n                            <h5>Select Category</h5>\r\n                            <div className=\"category\" >\r\n                              <input className=\"checkbox\" type=\"checkbox\" onClick={handleAllChecked}  value=\"checkedall\" /> Check / Uncheck All\r\n                                <ul>\r\n                                {\r\n                                  categories.map(category => {\r\n                                    return (<span>\r\n                                      {category.hasChildren \r\n                                        ? <span><CheckBox key={category._id} \r\n                                        handleCheckChieldElement={handleCheckChieldElement}  {...category} />\r\n                                        <ul>\r\n                                          {\r\n                                          category.children.map(child => {\r\n                                            return (\r\n                                              <h5>\r\n                                                {\r\n                                                categories.sort().map(childCategory => {\r\n                                                return (<span>{\r\n                                                  childCategory.slug === child \r\n                                                  ? <CheckBox key={childCategory._id} handleCheckChieldElement={handleCheckChieldElement}  {...childCategory} />\r\n                                                  : \"\"\r\n                                                }</span>)                                       \r\n                                              })\r\n                                            }\r\n                                            </h5>\r\n                                            )\r\n                                          })\r\n                                        }   \r\n                                        </ul>\r\n                                        </span>                          \r\n                                        : category.isChild ? \"\" : <CheckBox key={category._id} handleCheckChieldElement={handleCheckChieldElement}  {...category} />\r\n                                      }\r\n                                    </span>)\r\n                                  })\r\n                                }\r\n                                </ul>\r\n                            </div>\r\n\r\n                            <main>\r\n                              <ImageSelector show={show} handleClose={hideModal} setFeaturedImage={setFeaturedImage}/>\r\n                              <button className=\"featuredimage\" type=\"button\" onClick={showModal}>\r\n                                  Featured Image\r\n                              </button><br/><br/>\r\n                              <img src={imagepath} alt=''></img><br/>\r\n                              <label>Image Caption: {imagecaption}</label><br/>\r\n                            </main>\r\n\r\n                            <label>Publish Date</label> <DatePicker\r\n                            className=\"datepicker\"\r\n                                selected={date}\r\n                                onChange={onChangeDate}\r\n                            />\r\n                            <label>Status:{poststatus}</label>\r\n                            <button className=\"draftbutton\" onClick={(e) => {e.preventDefault();savePost(true)}} >\r\n                                Save as draft\r\n                            </button>\r\n                            <button className=\"publishbutton\" onClick={(e) => {e.preventDefault();savePost(false)}}>\r\n                                Publish\r\n                            </button>\r\n                          </div><br/>\r\n                      </form>\r\n                  </div>\r\n          </div>\r\n        )\r\n    }\r\n\r\n\r\n    export default AddPost", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 0, "reactions_total": 0, "reactions_plus": 0, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "Shawan1008", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2020-03-11T12:09:11Z", "updated_at": "2022-06-28T06:25:37Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/10968", "classification": "need-related"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 10970, "title": "How to get the protocol(origin) in getInitialProps?", "body": "We need to display the origin on our page. But we find that it is no way to get the protocol (http or https) on server side in `getInitialProps`.\r\n\r\nThen we find `next-absolute-url`. But it can only deal with 'localhost'. If we add '127.0.0.1 www.aaa.com' into host file and we type '**http**://www.aaa.com/' in  browser, we get **https** returned by `next-absolute-url`.\r\n\r\nSo, is there a easy way to get the true protocol(origin) in `getInitialProps` (return exactly the same to location.protocol on client side)?", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "closed", "state_reason": "resolved", "comments": 0, "reactions_total": 0, "reactions_plus": 0, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "jim-king-2000", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2020-03-11T13:32:15Z", "updated_at": "2023-10-27T01:46:33Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/10970", "classification": "need-related"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 10977, "title": "Pass additional data from getStaticPaths to getStaticProps", "body": "Hi,\r\n\r\nIs it possible to return additional data in the `getStaticPaths()` response? And read that in `getStaticProps(context)`\r\n\r\nFor example \r\n```\r\n{ \r\n  paths: [{ params: { slug: ['content'], data: 'extra' } }], \r\n  fallback: false \r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nCurrently the `context` parameter in `getStaticProps()` is just \r\n\r\n```\r\n{ params: { slug: [ 'content' ] } }\r\n```\r\n\r\nWe would like to fetch data from our CMS by ID in `getStaticProps`, but show a different slug.", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 3, "reactions_total": 42, "reactions_plus": 42, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "arthurvi", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2020-03-11T15:38:03Z", "updated_at": "2022-06-01T13:24:37Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/10977", "classification": "random"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 10979, "title": "subdomain routing without conflicts", "body": "Let's say my app has `team` entity, `post` entity and `category`\r\n\r\nPossible routes\r\n\r\n`https://team1.app.com/post1`\r\n`https://team2.app.com/post2`\r\n\r\nbut also `https://app.com/cateogory1/post3` where `post3` is public in my app so can be accessed without the team.\r\n\r\nI understand subdomain parsing is not part of next.js core for security reasons, but in example above first segment after `app.com` can mean either post or category, depending on if subdomain is used or not.\r\n\r\nIs it possible to handle such case in next?", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 3, "reactions_total": 0, "reactions_plus": 0, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "pie6k", "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR", "created_at": "2020-03-11T16:02:47Z", "updated_at": "2022-09-02T18:03:54Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/10979", "classification": "random"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 10988, "title": "SSG and SSR errors while deploying to `zeit/now`", "body": "```\r\nModule not found: Can't resolve 'dns' in '/zeit/fa3e271/node_modules/mongodb/lib'\r\n00:11:08.674\r\n> Build error occurred\r\n00:11:08.675\r\nError: > Build failed because of webpack errors\r\n00:11:08.675\r\n```\r\n\r\nGetting now that error on the deployment to now that seems related to executing the db function call on the `getStaticProps` function of the component. Any leads on how to deploy now? Works perfectly on local with `next` on local\r\n\r\n", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 1, "reactions_total": 0, "reactions_plus": 0, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "mgranados", "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR", "created_at": "2020-03-12T06:35:54Z", "updated_at": "2022-10-19T13:54:32Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/10988", "classification": "need-related"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 10989, "title": "Is duplicate files when exporting with exportTrailingSlash intended?", "body": "This post heavily references this closed bug:\r\nhttps://github.com/zeit/next.js/issues/8119\r\n\r\nI found the above GitHub issue when searching for an answer to that question. I implemented the solution mentioned by @devisscher (utilizing exportTrailingSlash) but as @jaredpereira noted, this results in more files than (at least I) expected being created: \r\n\r\nNotably, in my project:\r\n`out/index.html` and  `out/index/index.html`\r\n`out/404.html` and  `out/404/index.html`\r\n\r\n<img width=\"192\" alt=\"Screen Shot 2020-03-12 at 12 41 08 AM\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/12590512/76494312-2ca1da80-63fa-11ea-909d-8c03130433f3.png\">\r\n\r\n@Timer mentioned something was [intended behavior](https://github.com/zeit/next.js/issues/8119#issuecomment-521645127) but I'm not sure if they were referring to these duplicate files or just that \"An index file does not imply a trailing slash\".\r\n\r\nIs my output described about actually intended? If so, is there a way to get a `/about` type of route without getting duplicate pages?\r\n\r\nThanks!", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 2, "reactions_total": 0, "reactions_plus": 0, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "davidprae", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2020-03-12T06:52:20Z", "updated_at": "2023-01-16T16:09:22Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/10989", "classification": "random"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 10990, "title": "Dynamic routes with SSR lead to 404 pages on visit", "body": "# Bug report\r\n\r\n## Describe the bug\r\n\r\nI have a nextjs application, which supports pretty url like: <https://demo.oga.fit/balance> or <https://demo.oga.fit/balance/diva-yoga>. It is exported to work behind gitlab pages.\r\n\r\nThe slugs are loaded from the backend over a request. The [home page][home] lists them. When going from the home page to the slug based URL, the pages are working. However, if I refresh the browser when already on the above mentioned URL, it shows a 404 page instead.\r\n\r\n## To Reproduce\r\n\r\nSteps to reproduce the behavior, please provide code snippets or a repository:\r\n\r\n1. Go to <https://demo.oga.fit/>\r\n2. Click on `Balance` or `Learn` images shown\r\n3. After the page is rendered, refresh the browser tab. It should display a 404 error on refresh.\r\n\r\n## Expected behavior\r\n\r\nInstead of the 404 page, I'd assume that the dynamic routes would come into play and render the actual content.\r\n\r\n## Additional context\r\n\r\nIt is a closed source application; I'd not be able to share code snippets.\r\n\r\n  [home]: https://demo.oga.fit/", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 4, "reactions_total": 0, "reactions_plus": 0, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "hjpotter92", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2020-03-12T07:04:35Z", "updated_at": "2022-06-07T22:20:16Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/10990", "classification": "random"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 10992, "title": "Circular references cannot be expressed in JSON.", "body": "Hey guys, I faced some issues when using `getServerSideProps` on 9.3. I fetched some data using apollo graphql and pass it to the page. but i got following error.\r\n```\r\nError serializing `.mixes.items[2].user` returned from `getServerSideProps` in \"/\". Reason: Circular references cannot be expressed in JSON.\r\nError: Error serializing `.mixes.items[2].user` returned from `getServerSideProps` in \"/\".\r\nReason: Circular references cannot be expressed in JSON.\r\n    at visit (/Users/zorig/xyyp/play/node_modules/next/dist/lib/is-serializable-props.js:1:668)\r\n    at isSerializable (/Users/zorig/xyyp/play/node_modules/next/dist/lib/is-serializable-props.js:7:256)\r\n    at /Users/zorig/xyyp/play/node_modules/next/dist/lib/is-serializable-props.js:7:456\r\n```\r\n\r\nmy fetched data looks like the following:\r\n```\r\n mixes: {\r\n    items:[\r\n        {\r\n          __typename: \"Mix\",\r\n          id: \"1\",\r\n          title: \"\u0425\u0438\u043f \u0425\u043e\u043f \u0445\u0438\u0442 \u0434\u0443\u0443\u043d\u0443\u0443\u0434\",\r\n          thumb: \"https://localhost:8000/media/mix/hhrnb.jpg\",\r\n          user: {\r\n            __typename: \"User\",\r\n            id: \"1\",\r\n            name: \"User1\"\r\n          }\r\n        },\r\n      {\r\n          __typename: \"Mix\",\r\n          id: \"2\",\r\n          title: \"Dance EDM\",\r\n          thumb: \"https://localhost:8000/media/dance_mix.jpg\",\r\n          user: {\r\n            __typename: \"User\",\r\n            id: \"2\",\r\n            name: \"User2\"\r\n          }\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          __typename: \"Mix\",\r\n          id: \"4\",\r\n          title: \"Acoustic Vibes\",\r\n          thumb: \"https://localhost:8000/media/Acoustic_vibes_mix.jpg\",\r\n          user: {\r\n            __typename: \"User\",\r\n            id: \"2\",\r\n            name: \"User2\"\r\n          }\r\n        },\r\n    ]\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nand i tried to run inspection and run `is-serializable-props` on my fetched data.\r\n\r\n```javascript\r\nimport { isSerializableProps } from \"next/dist/lib/is-serializable-props\";\r\n    isSerializableProps(\"adasd\", \"asdasd\", {\r\n      props: {\r\n         mixes\r\n      }\r\n```\r\nwhich throws the exact same error. But when i hardcoded data inside props, it does not throw an error\r\n\r\nI even checked by data by  `isPlainObject` from lodash and it shows true. ", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 26, "reactions_total": 0, "reactions_plus": 0, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "Zorig", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2020-03-12T08:09:59Z", "updated_at": "2023-04-12T14:09:43Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/10992", "classification": "need-related"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 10994, "title": "Transpiling / Polyfilling with Next.js 9.3", "body": "Hi!\r\nFrom the  [announcement blog post of version 9.3](https://nextjs.org/blog/next-9-3) I can see that the framework will now handle split bundles into module/no-module versions, with polyfills added to the no-module version.\r\n\r\n### Question\r\nIs it still necessary to add own polyfills/transpile code with babel afterwards? At the moment, we use [next-transpile-modules](https://github.com/martpie/next-transpile-modules) to transpile specific node-modules, and use this `babel.config.js` to transpile out application code:\r\n\r\n```js\r\nmodule.exports = {\r\n\tplugins: [],\r\n\tenv: {\r\n\t\tdevelopment: {\r\n\t\t\tpresets: [\"next/babel\"],\r\n\t\t},\r\n\t\tproduction: {\r\n\t\t\tcomments: false,\r\n\t\t\tpresets: [\r\n\t\t\t\t[\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\"next/babel\",\r\n\t\t\t\t\t{\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\"preset-env\": {\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tdebug: true,\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tuseBuiltIns: \"usage\",\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\"transform-runtime\": {},\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\"styled-jsx\": {},\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\"class-properties\": {},\r\n\t\t\t\t\t},\r\n\t\t\t\t],\r\n\t\t\t],\r\n\t\t\tplugins: [\"@babel/plugin-transform-arrow-functions\"],\r\n\t\t},\r\n\t\ttest: {\r\n\t\t\tpresets: [\"next/babel\"],\r\n\t\t},\r\n\t},\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nWill this actually make the situation worse? Would appreciate to have some information about this topic! We need to support IE11 \ud83d\ude45\u200d\u2642 .\r\n\r\n### Documentation\r\nIt would be nice to add the topics **transpiling** and **polyfilling** to the Next.js documentation. **I would like help with this** for sure if someone who knows more about this will point me to the correct resources.\r\n\r\nThanks for the great work with the new update, keep it up \ud83d\udc4d ", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 13, "reactions_total": 0, "reactions_plus": 0, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "danlutz", "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR", "created_at": "2020-03-12T09:22:36Z", "updated_at": "2022-06-21T17:26:35Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/10994", "classification": "random"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 10996, "title": "fork-ts-checker-webpack-plugin seems to create a lot of zombie child processes", "body": "Almost 20 of the running node processes are `fork-ts-checker-webpack-plugin` and it making my development experience terrible because my computer of 12gb RAM kept on running out of RAM memory every now and then\r\n\r\n![Screenshot from 2020-03-12 11 02 18](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/25849232/76510119-618d4c00-6451-11ea-8dcb-18732ab6a4a5.png)\r\n\r\nIs there anything that I can to stop this?", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 0, "reactions_total": 0, "reactions_plus": 0, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "Akumzy", "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR", "created_at": "2020-03-12T10:10:28Z", "updated_at": "2022-10-13T19:45:32Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/10996", "classification": "need-related"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 11002, "title": "Dynamic Routes only load client-side on Zeit Now", "body": "Hey, my dynamic routes work fine locally, but when I deploy my project to Zeit Now, server-side rendering of my dynamice routes doesn't work and I get the `404: NOT_FOUND` screen from Now. \r\n\r\nThey work however when accessed through the client-side.\r\n\r\nI will be happy to provide additional info.\r\n\r\n", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 5, "reactions_total": 0, "reactions_plus": 0, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "BjoernRave", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2020-03-12T13:18:34Z", "updated_at": "2023-01-23T11:39:21Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/11002", "classification": "random"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 11007, "title": "Scripts in _document.js.", "body": "How to solve the problem of an external script in _document? . The script is added after NextScript  but nevertheless does not work. The same script runs fine in React.\r\n\r\n```\r\n<body>\r\n  <Main />\r\n  <Preloader />\r\n  <NextScript />\r\n  <script type=\"text/javascript\" dangerouslySetInnerHTML={this.WindowPreloader()} />\r\n  <script type=\"text/javascript\" src=\"https://widgets.radioheart.ru/static/js/manifest.js\" />\r\n  <script type=\"text/javascript\" src=\"https://widgets.radioheart.ru/static/js/vendor.js\" />\r\n  <script type=\"text/javascript\" src=\"https://widgets.radioheart.ru/static/js/app.js\" />\r\n  <script src=\"https://player.radioheart.ru/js/app.js\" />\r\n  <script src=\"https://www.google.com/recaptcha/api.js?onload=onloadCallback&render=explicit\" async defer />\r\n</body>\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\n", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 9, "reactions_total": 0, "reactions_plus": 0, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "FReeeZzze", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2020-03-12T17:03:45Z", "updated_at": "2023-08-04T05:03:42Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/11007", "classification": "need-related"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 11009, "title": "getServerSideProps is ignored", "body": "Given the following code it looks like getServerSideProps is ignored completely.\r\n\r\n```javascript\r\nimport React from \"react\";\r\nimport Layout from \"../../components/Layout\";\r\n\r\nfunction Post(props) {\r\n  console.log(\"in render\");\r\n  return (\r\n    <Layout title={\"post title\"}>\r\n      <pre>{JSON.stringify(props, undefined, 2)}</pre>\r\n      {/* this shows\r\n          {\r\n            \"url\": {\r\n              \"query\": {\r\n                \"id\": \"8\"\r\n              },\r\n              \"pathname\": \"/post/[id]\",\r\n              \"asPath\": \"/post/8\"\r\n            }\r\n          }      \r\n      */}\r\n    </Layout>\r\n  );\r\n}\r\n\r\nexport async function getServerSideProps(needQuery) {\r\n  console.log(\"never see this\", needQuery);\r\n  return { props: { dosNot: \"matter, never called\" } };\r\n}\r\n\r\nexport default Post;\r\n```\r\n\r\nOn the server it logs \"in render\" once and on the client it logs \"in render\" twice and one warning about accessing the url property once on server and client.\r\n\r\nI am using next version [9.3.0](https://github.com/harm-meijer/nextjs-example/blob/<HASH_REDACTED>/yarn.lock#L3760-L3760)\r\n\r\nFull code is [here](https://github.com/harm-meijer/nextjs-example/tree/refactor) (refactor branch) and I start it with `yarn dev`.\r\n\r\nJust noticed that not only does it not work, it also breaks single page application and causes a page reload when navigating from list of posts to single post, that didn't happen in master branch.", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 2, "reactions_total": 0, "reactions_plus": 0, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "amsterdamharu", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2020-03-12T18:16:36Z", "updated_at": "2022-06-22T19:27:11Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/11009", "classification": "random"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 11013, "title": "Unable to import Html5 Navigator", "body": "# Bug report\r\n\r\n## Describe the bug\r\n\r\nI'm unable to use [Navigator](https://www.w3schools.com/html/html5_geolocation.asp), I'm getting:\r\n\r\n```\r\nReferenceError: navigator is not defined\r\n``` \r\n\r\n## To Reproduce\r\n\r\nSimple try to use native HTML5 navigator api.\r\n\r\n## Expected behavior\r\n\r\nBe able to access navigator\r\n\r\n## System information\r\n\r\n- OS: macOS\r\n- Browser (if applies): Chrome\r\n- Version of Next.js: 9.2.2\r\n", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 11, "reactions_total": 0, "reactions_plus": 0, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "samuelcastro", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2020-03-12T20:08:16Z", "updated_at": "2023-08-05T12:24:18Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/11013", "classification": "random"}
