{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 11342, "title": "API error in getStaticProps => build error?", "body": "I couldn't find anything about thrown errors in `getStaticProps` in the docs. For example when an API request fails. I hope that this would cause a build error?\r\n\r\nIf not, that could cause compiling an error into the static page undetected, being fatal on deployment. If it would cause a build error, still we would need to **not** use `try/catch` for API calls, otherwise we would run into the same issue.\r\n\r\nhttps://nextjs.org/docs/basic-features/data-fetching#getstaticprops-static-generation", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 2, "reactions_total": 0, "reactions_plus": 0, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "fabb", "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR", "created_at": "2020-03-25T08:00:48Z", "updated_at": "2022-06-03T07:37:49Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/11342", "classification": "random"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 11346, "title": "How to Redirect in getStaticProps", "body": "Hi, I need to check the existence of a JWT token to navigate the user to the correct route. I put my token validation stuff in `getStaticProps` function. How can I redirect the user to another route in `getStaticProps` function? I have tried this, but it's not working:\r\n\r\n```ts\r\nasync (context: NextPageContext): Promise<{ props: { token: string } }> => {\r\n  const { token } = nextCookies(context);\r\n  console.log(context) // {}\r\n  if (!token) {\r\n    if (typeof window === 'undefined') {\r\n      // \u274c I get no 'res' key on context for redirection so this throws an error\r\n      context.res.writeHead(302, { Location: '/phone-get' });\r\n      context.res.end();\r\n    } else {\r\n      /* \u274c\r\n        this wouldn't work as well. Because the router is not available here.\r\n        The next router only works on the client side\r\n      */\r\n      Router.replace('/phone-get');\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  return {\r\n    props: { token },\r\n  };\r\n};\r\n```", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 30, "reactions_total": 3, "reactions_plus": 3, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "Kiarash-Z", "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR", "created_at": "2020-03-25T17:27:15Z", "updated_at": "2023-03-27T07:25:40Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/11346", "classification": "need-related"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 11351, "title": "No Firebase App '[DEFAULT]' has been created - call Firebase App.initializeApp() (app/no-app)", "body": "I'm getting that error when calling firebase in `getInitialProps` or `getStaticProps`.\r\n\r\n```\r\nPage.getInitialProps = async ({ req }) => {\r\nconst db = await firebase.firestore(); // firebase is not ready yet\r\n...\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe issue seems to be that whatever call is being made is happening before `initializeApp()` is complete. In the [with-firebase](https://github.com/zeit/next.js/blob/canary/examples/with-firebase/firebase/clientApp.js), firebase is just configured and exported. So I guess it needs to loaded async somehow. \r\n\r\nAnyone have a solution for this? ", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 9, "reactions_total": 4, "reactions_plus": 4, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "stormfar", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2020-03-25T19:51:12Z", "updated_at": "2022-11-22T09:45:21Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/11351", "classification": "random"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 11352, "title": "Next.js SSR not working", "body": "Hello everyone, I use next.js with redux + redux thunk. I am working on the action and rendering the value component. There is no error in my code, but when I look at the source code, there is no value rendered.\r\n\r\nPlease, help me fix the error.\r\n\r\nAction: https://github.com/Phoique/save-movies/blob/master/next-ssr/actions/myMovies.js\r\n\r\nReducer: https://github.com/Phoique/save-movies/blob/master/next-ssr/reducers/myMoviesReducer.js\r\n\r\nComponent: https://github.com/Phoique/save-movies/blob/master/next-ssr/pages/mymovies.js", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 0, "reactions_total": 0, "reactions_plus": 0, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "phoique", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2020-03-25T22:35:28Z", "updated_at": "2023-03-07T21:35:45Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/11352", "classification": "need-related"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 11354, "title": "Clarification on CSR (Specifically with Apollo)", "body": "Looking at the `with-apollo` example, we see that there is a demonstration of a \"client-only\" page: https://github.com/zeit/next.js/blob/canary/examples/with-apollo/pages/client-only.js\r\n\r\nHowever, when I run this example locally, and put a console log before returning the \"client only\" page jsx, I see that the console log prints on the server, which confuses me. How can I write a page so that it is truly only rendered on the client?", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 4, "reactions_total": 0, "reactions_plus": 0, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "bwesner", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2020-03-25T23:27:46Z", "updated_at": "2022-06-18T09:47:03Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/11354", "classification": "random"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 32238, "title": "Enable preview mode during development in an iframe", "body": "# Feature request\r\n\r\n## Is your feature request related to a problem? Please describe.\r\nStoryblok visual composer runs NextJS inside an IFrame. Due to this handling the cookie to enable preview mode is never set and the preview mode does not work for SSG handling.\r\n\r\n## Describe the solution you'd like\r\nProbably it would be a good idea if the preview mode could be enabled through URL params. The cookie solution might break other headless CMS systems as well\r\n\r\n## Describe alternatives you've considered\r\nAlternatively I'd like to run my site in SSR mode on a specific domain. It feels like a hack because I would need to deploy every project twice for each mode. \r\n", "category": "Ideas", "category_slug": "ideas", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 19, "reactions_total": 9, "reactions_plus": 9, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "dohomi", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2020-03-26T00:30:00Z", "updated_at": "2022-06-02T13:58:24Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/32238", "classification": "random"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 62351, "title": "[Feature Request] View the app \"On Your Network\"", "body": "### View the app \"On Your Network\"\r\n\r\nBy default create-react-app make the app live on `localhost` as well as your network.\r\nThis would make it easier to test on mobile devices. Also the current way has the text mixing in with all the other details and becomes harder to find. I would be better to highlight somehow, maybe draw a box around it.\r\n\r\nEdit: **I opened a PR to solve this #22352**\r\n\r\n```sh\r\n[ info ]  ready on http://localhost:3000\r\n```\r\n\r\n![react](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/18533307/77638763-af3fa380-6f7d-11ea-8ecb-fdc8115dab4b.jpeg)\r\n", "category": "Ideas", "category_slug": "ideas", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 24, "reactions_total": 73, "reactions_plus": 51, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 6, "reactions_confused": 1, "reactions_heart": 5, "reactions_rocket": 7, "reactions_eyes": 3, "author": "heyitsarpit", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2020-03-26T10:59:42Z", "updated_at": "2024-02-21T22:42:37Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/62351", "classification": "need-related"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 11375, "title": "exportPathMap for /pages/api", "body": "Next has a built in API route\r\nhttps://nextjs.org/docs/api-routes/introduction\r\n\r\nbut it uses `/pages/api`\r\n\r\nIs it possible to change the default path from `/api/*` to something else like `/myApi/*`?\r\n\r\nI was thinking about adding it to exportPathMap\r\nhttps://nextjs.org/docs/api-reference/next.config.js/exportPathMap\r\n\r\nAny suggestions?", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 1, "reactions_total": 0, "reactions_plus": 0, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "leon-do", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2020-03-26T18:47:53Z", "updated_at": "2022-06-09T08:11:51Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/11375", "classification": "random"}
