{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 11413, "title": "Is it a good idea to use Next.js with react-native-web?", "body": "I looked at the [nextjs react-native-web example](https://github.com/zeit/next.js/tree/canary/examples/with-react-native-web). I wonder which are the trade-off of implementing this?\r\n\r\nI assume that the app would lose the nextjs routing with `next/router` and `<Link>`.\r\nAlso I assume that all the style-jsx, css and sass features would be lost.\r\nHow would code-splitting and all the other nextjs goodies would be affected?\r\n", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 1, "reactions_total": 0, "reactions_plus": 0, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "vasco3", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2020-03-27T19:50:55Z", "updated_at": "2024-04-25T15:49:09Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/11413", "classification": "random"}
