{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 11443, "title": "Next.js public roadmap", "body": "Is there a public roadmap somewhere?\r\n\r\nIf so, is it possible to add some ROADMAP.md in the repo that point towards whatever exists?\r\n\r\nHaving an overview of where the framework is going would be nice, a 3-6 months visibility would be great.", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 1, "reactions_total": 13, "reactions_plus": 13, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "Vadorequest", "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR", "created_at": "2020-03-28T20:04:19Z", "updated_at": "2022-06-10T12:25:16Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/11443", "classification": "need-related"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 11445, "title": "don't show photos after production in next.js", "body": "I made an application with Next.js and used node.js in the api part. I had no problems using it on my own computer, but when I run it on my server in digitalocean, the photos I uploaded from the administration panel are not shown. When I check the database and directory, there is no problem. The photo is being recorded there. section is correct when I enter the site and check it. When I wear path / file.jpg it gives 404 error.\r\n\r\nThere is no problem in the previous recordings and it shows the photos. The photos do not show after running on the server.\r\n\r\nI made folder permissions 777, but nothing else came to my mind. I didn't add code because I didn't think there was a problem with the code.", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 1, "reactions_total": 0, "reactions_plus": 0, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "berat", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2020-03-28T20:45:00Z", "updated_at": "2022-07-31T16:37:20Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/11445", "classification": "random"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 11450, "title": "Error in _error.tsx vs _app.tsx with componentDidCatch", "body": "Hi, I would like to know the difference between\r\n- `_app` with componentDidCatch(err) { ... }\r\n- `_error` with getInitialProps({ err }) { ... }\r\n\r\nand where should I put my code for error logger (I'm using Sentry) ?", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 0, "reactions_total": 1, "reactions_plus": 1, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "Fonger", "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR", "created_at": "2020-03-28T23:47:19Z", "updated_at": "2023-03-02T10:34:46Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/11450", "classification": "need-related"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 11451, "title": "Next.js + react-native-web + (styled-components OR emotion)", "body": "This combination of packages is very shaky. Both [`emotion`](https://emotion.sh/docs/@emotion/native#example) and [`styled-components`](https://styled-components.com/docs/basics#react-native) run into\r\n\r\n`Error: Cannot find module 'react-native'`\r\n\r\nwith `react-native-web`. I am not sure yet what exactly is going on and how to fix it. Looks like I need to tell babel / webpack to alias the \"react-native\" package to \"react-native-web\" inside `node_modules/styled-components` / `node_modules/@emotion/native`.\r\n\r\nI will look into it ASAP, if anyone has another idea, I'd greatly appreciate it. Would be also cool to have this extended in the [`with-react-native-web`](https://github.com/zeit/next.js/tree/master/examples/with-react-native-web) example\r\n\r\nOther places talking about it:\r\n\r\n- https://github.com/emotion-js/emotion/issues/1199\r\n- https://github.com/styled-components/styled-components/issues/2624 (partly related)", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 0, "reactions_total": 6, "reactions_plus": 6, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "mxmzb", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2020-03-29T00:07:12Z", "updated_at": "2024-07-26T20:23:42Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/11451", "classification": "random"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 11456, "title": "Cannot not run getServersideProps", "body": "I made an attempt at this in  #11453, however I don\u2019t think I\u2019m there (the PR also addresses a different bug, \u201cshallow routing never happens unless the new route is the existing route\u201d)\n\nI haven\u2019t found a way to not run getServersideProps. Even if a route is cached, there is no way to disable it from running.\n\nIs this by design?", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 0, "reactions_total": 0, "reactions_plus": 0, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "samschooler", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2020-03-29T05:33:53Z", "updated_at": "2023-10-26T21:03:13Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/11456", "classification": "random"}
