{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 11464, "title": "Throwing 404 from getStaticProps fallback", "body": "Is it possible to throw a 404 (with the correct status code) from inside the fallback of getStaticProps?\r\n\r\nThe page works as expected: it renders a list of 10 forecasts at build time, and the fallback loads any that aren't pre rendered, and displays the error page when none are found. But when the error page is displayed, it doesn't give a 404 response, it's all 200 OK.\r\n\r\nMaybe this is a misuse of getStaticProps, and is an example of when to switch to SSR instead?\r\n\r\n```\r\nimport fetch from \"node-fetch\";\r\nimport { useRouter } from \"next/router\";\r\n\r\nimport ErrorPage from \"next/error\";\r\nimport Layout from \"components/Layout.js\";\r\n\r\nfunction Forecast({ forecast }) {\r\n  const router = useRouter();\r\n\r\n  if (forecast && forecast.error != undefined) {\r\n    return <ErrorPage statusCode={404} />;\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  const buildOutput = props => {\r\n    if (router.isFallback) {\r\n      return <div>Loading...</div>;\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    return (\r\n      <>\r\n        <h1>{forecast.title}</h1>\r\n        <p>...</p>\r\n      </>\r\n    );\r\n  };\r\n\r\n  return (\r\n    <>\r\n      <Layout>{buildOutput()}</Layout>\r\n    </>\r\n  );\r\n}\r\n\r\nexport async function getStaticPaths() {\r\n  const res = await fetch(\"https://...forecasts\");\r\n  const forecasts = await res.json();\r\n\r\n  const paths = forecasts.map(forecast => `/forecasts/${forecast.hash}`);\r\n\r\n  return { paths, fallback: true };\r\n}\r\n\r\nexport async function getStaticProps({ params }) {\r\n  const res = await fetch(`https://...forecasts/${params.hash}`);\r\n  const forecast = await res.json();\r\n\r\n  return { props: { forecast } };\r\n}\r\n\r\nexport default Forecast;\r\n```\r\n", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 5, "reactions_total": 4, "reactions_plus": 4, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "bradders", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2020-03-29T17:14:05Z", "updated_at": "2024-03-13T18:53:22Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/11464", "classification": "random"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 11466, "title": "[9.1.7] How to embed a script using Head?", "body": "As I understand from my [SO question ](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/60918188/how-do-i-use-embed-code-in-react-with-hooks/60918371?noredirect=1#comment107776693_60918371), I can use next/head to embed a script tag within a component of my React / Next JS app. So, I went about it as such:\r\n```\r\nimport React, { Component } from \"react\";\r\n...\r\nimport Head from \"next/head\";\r\nexport const Lead = props => {\r\n  return (\r\n...\r\n        <Head>\r\n          <script\r\n            class=\"3758abc\"\r\n            type=\"text/javascript\"\r\n            src=\"https://cdn2.fake.com/Scripts/embed-button.min.js\"\r\n            data-encoded=\"1234sdkljfeiASD9A\"\r\n          ></script>\r\n        </Head>\r\n...\r\n  );\r\n};\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Unfortunately, nothing rendered.** I don't know if I'm missing something obvious here...\r\nI'm using Next 9.1.7.\r\n\r\nMy _app.js looks like this:\r\n```\r\nimport App, { Container } from \"next/app\";\r\nimport Page from \"../components/Page\";\r\nimport { ApolloProvider } from \"react-apollo\";\r\nimport withData from \"../lib/withData\";\r\n\r\nclass MyApp extends App {\r\n  static async getInitialProps({ Component, ctx }) {\r\n    let pageProps = {};\r\n    if (Component.getInitialProps) {\r\n      pageProps = await Component.getInitialProps(ctx);\r\n    }\r\n    // this exposes the query to the user\r\n    pageProps.query = ctx.query;\r\n    return { pageProps };\r\n  }\r\n  render() {\r\n    const { Component, apollo, pageProps } = this.props;\r\n\r\n    return (\r\n      // <Container>\r\n      <ApolloProvider client={apollo}>\r\n        <Page>\r\n          <Component {...pageProps} />\r\n        </Page>\r\n      </ApolloProvider>\r\n      // </Container>\r\n    );\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n\r\nexport default withData(MyApp);\r\n```\r\nAnd my _document looks like this:\r\n```\r\nimport Document from \"next/document\";\r\nimport { ServerStyleSheet } from \"styled-components\";\r\n\r\nexport default class MyDocument extends Document {\r\n  static getInitialProps = async ctx => {\r\n    const sheet = new ServerStyleSheet();\r\n    const originalRenderPage = ctx.renderPage;\r\n\r\n    try {\r\n      ctx.renderPage = () =>\r\n        originalRenderPage({\r\n          enhanceApp: App => props => sheet.collectStyles(<App {...props} />)\r\n        });\r\n\r\n      const initialProps = await Document.getInitialProps(ctx);\r\n      return {\r\n        ...initialProps,\r\n        styles: (\r\n          <>\r\n            {initialProps.styles}\r\n            {sheet.getStyleElement()}\r\n          </>\r\n        )\r\n      };\r\n    } finally {\r\n      sheet.seal();\r\n    }\r\n  };\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\n", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 1, "reactions_total": 0, "reactions_plus": 0, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "hatchli", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2020-03-29T18:54:08Z", "updated_at": "2022-07-04T14:34:37Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/11466", "classification": "need-related"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 11475, "title": "getStaticProps with Pagination", "body": "First of all, the static blog starter with tailwind example is great! I've been toying around with it, and I'm not sure how to go about pre-rendering paginated static pages. Do you have any plans to to include something like that in the example, or does anyone have a repo example with this feature?", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 2, "reactions_total": 0, "reactions_plus": 0, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "joshuaoas", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2020-03-30T02:42:28Z", "updated_at": "2022-06-05T11:59:27Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/11475", "classification": "random"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 11481, "title": "getStaticPaths, getStaticProps, ssrCache", "body": "Error [ERR_HTTP_HEADERS_SENT]: Cannot set headers after they are sent to the client\r\n\r\nthis is what  am getting when am using ssrCaching example\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/zeit/next.js/tree/canary/examples/ssr-caching\r\n\r\nI had to change one line in server.js\r\n\r\nfrom \r\n```\r\nconst pagePath = '/blog';\r\n```\r\nto\r\n```\r\nconst pagePath = `/blog/${req.params.id}`;\r\n```\r\nin order to make refresh work\r\n\r\nbut it resulted in receiving the mentioned error\r\n\r\nif I swap to getInitialProps\r\nit works without any error\r\n\r\ndoes it have anything to do with caching built inside SSG?", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 1, "reactions_total": 0, "reactions_plus": 0, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "mohux", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2020-03-30T08:18:00Z", "updated_at": "2022-10-17T16:48:23Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/11481", "classification": "random"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 11483, "title": "How to reduce the size of commons.js in Next 8?", "body": "How to reduce the size of commons.js?\r\nnext.js version: 8.0.3\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/25126224/77908709-948f6680-72be-11ea-9fc3-1b3a2a1371ff.png)\r\nSize: 185K", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 6, "reactions_total": 0, "reactions_plus": 0, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "wq93", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2020-03-30T10:17:52Z", "updated_at": "2022-08-30T08:15:46Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/11483", "classification": "random"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 11484, "title": "`router.query` returns undefined parameter on first render in Next.js", "body": "When I have the following code and visit `/pages/profile/foo`, the page gets rendered twice and the first time `router.query.user` is `undefined`.\r\n\r\nIn file `/pages/profile/[user].js`\r\n\r\n```jsx\r\nimport { useRouter } from \"next/router\"\r\n\r\nexport default () => {\r\n  const router = useRouter()\r\n  const { user } = router.query\r\n  console.log(user)\r\n\r\n  return <p>User is {user}</p>\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nI will get 2 console logs - first is `undefined`, then the correct `foo`.\r\n\r\nCan anyone explain to me why is this happening?", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 139, "reactions_total": 145, "reactions_plus": 145, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "rasperrypie", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2020-03-30T10:24:42Z", "updated_at": "2025-12-13T18:12:09Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/11484", "classification": "need-related"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 11487, "title": "handling query params for getStaticPaths", "body": "#### The issue:\r\n`getStaticPaths` right now only works for actual routes like `/blog/page/[page]`. I'd like to use it with query params like `/blog?page=1`. \r\n\r\n#### Solutions I considered:\r\n - making the entire thing the param (`/[blogWithQuery] -> /blog?page=1`), but that would prevent me from putting another dynamic page at the root (like `/[gender]/products`)\r\n - putting the query parameter into the route param (`/blog/[query] -> /blog/?page=1`) but that's a bit unusual and I had clients complain about it.\r\n - fetching pages dynamically or at run time, but that leads to slowdowns or worse ux.\r\n\r\nAre there any recommended, or alternative methods for handling this?", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 3, "reactions_total": 5, "reactions_plus": 5, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "csenio", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2020-03-30T11:17:25Z", "updated_at": "2025-03-12T14:14:45Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/11487", "classification": "need-related"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 11488, "title": "Cannot find module '../lib/load-env-config' after upgrading to 9.3.2", "body": "Hey!\r\nDue to this https://twitter.com/zeithq/status/1243265976361156608, I'm trying to upgrade to 9.3.2.\r\n\r\nHowever, after upgrading, our app does not start, because of a missing dependency:\r\n\r\n```\r\nnode_modules/next/types/index.d.ts:8:21 - error TS2307: Cannot find module '../lib/load-env-config'.\r\n\r\n8 import { Env } from '../lib/load-env-config'\r\n                      ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\r\n```\r\n\r\n```\r\nyarn why load-env-config\r\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\r\n\r\nyarn why v1.21.1\r\n[1/4] Why do we have the module \"load-env-config\"...?\r\n[2/4] Initialising dependency graph...\r\n[3/4] Finding dependency...\r\nerror We couldn't find a match!\r\n```\r\n\r\nAny clue about why this happens and how to resolve this?\r\n\r\n", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 7, "reactions_total": 0, "reactions_plus": 0, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "olpeh", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2020-03-30T12:04:06Z", "updated_at": "2022-06-20T01:05:34Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/11488", "classification": "need-related"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 11489, "title": "Debug server rendered styled-jsx vs client-side rendered jsx", "body": "Summary: our \"hero\" component has two states; initially it gets fed with nulls and undefineds while the data/text is loading and then as the data has loaded, it renders the images and text in the data. We are using apollo-client with SSR, so it does a double-pass over the React tree to 1) trigger the download of the headless CMS data and 2) render the React tree with hydrated data.\r\n\r\nHowever, **on one of our pages (only one of them) we have this error on load**:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1313\" alt=\"index.js:1 Warning: Prop className did not match Server jsx-349921261 Client jsx-4280868776\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/193115/77906903-08af1780-7289-11ea-858d-6f4ed74a409d.png\"> \r\n\r\n> index.js:1 Warning: Prop `className` did not match. Server: \"jsx-349921261\" Client: \"jsx-4280868776\"\r\n\r\nAll other pages work, but the data is obviously different between them. **How do I debug what causes the different jsx class to be applied?** I get good output from the server (as far as I can ascertain) but this causes a re-load of all the headless CMS data on the client, probably because the React tree can't properly re-hydrate.\r\n\r\nThe code in question looks like this rendered:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1317\" alt=\"Screenshot 2020-03-30 at 13 20 10\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/193115/77907005-3300d500-7289-11ea-84db-53acd4aa25af.png\">\r\n\r\nAnd this in source form (Appendix A).\r\n\r\n## React messes up box tracking\r\nThis wouldn't be a super-huge issue, hadn't it affected the layout in a very strange way; when the above warning happens, **react messes up and loses track of the content in two boxes**, so that it looks like this:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"888\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/193115/77911349-f9cc6300-7290-11ea-80f1-d9fc203c2d55.png\">\r\n\r\nWhen it really should look like:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"894\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/193115/77911406-0bae0600-7291-11ea-95b8-16e6b833a277.png\">\r\n\r\n(which it does when client-side navigating to it)\r\n\r\nHow do I debug/resolve this?\r\n\r\n\r\n#### Appendix A - Source code\r\n<img width=\"682\" alt=\"Screenshot 2020-03-30 at 13 20 52\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/193115/77907307-b5899480-7289-11ea-8484-b428da3e21dd.png\">\r\n\r\n#### Appendix B\r\n\r\nCross posted here https://stackoverflow.com/questions/60932324/debug-server-rendered-styled-jsx-vs-client-side-rendered-jsx", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 0, "reactions_total": 0, "reactions_plus": 0, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "haf", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2020-03-30T12:16:43Z", "updated_at": "2022-06-14T18:10:45Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/11489", "classification": "need-related"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 11491, "title": "Passing server-sided data with custom server to page", "body": "Hey there, sorry for asking a question that may have been asked multiple times already. But I am trying to make a sample project which uses [`oidc-provider` ](https://github.com/panva/node-oidc-provider) library. I'm all done with the OIDC configurations and only the frontend pages like login and authorization remaining to be developed, and I intend to use Next for this purpose. To follow their [example](https://github.com/panva/node-oidc-provider-example/blob/master/03-oidc-views-accounts/index.js), I need to use custom server to selectively render pages in a route. But problem is, now I could not find a way to pass the data from the express custom server which was obtained from `interactionDetails(req, res)` to my NextJS pages. I was thinking to use `query` parameter of Next's custom server `render` method to pass the data but then I've read about this usage being strongly discouraged and that it only supports string-(string | string[]) key-values with Typescript (I could probably `JSON.stringify` all the objects I want to pass in this case, but pretty sure this is basically hacking it). So, how can I pass the data properly from a custom server to my Next page?\r\n\r\nI haven't really tried using `getServerSideProps` but it seems I can't even import my OIDC instance in my Next pages and will error out if I do back with `getInitialProps` before v9.3. But then again in order to follow the example, I need to selectively render the page (if user is logged in, show authorization page, otherwise show login page first) which I don't know how to achieve with pages alone.", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 1, "reactions_total": 0, "reactions_plus": 0, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "ionizer", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2020-03-30T13:05:48Z", "updated_at": "2022-09-12T06:45:06Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/11491", "classification": "random"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 11493, "title": "getStaticPaths doesn't work with 'publicRuntimeConfig' from next/config", "body": "When I add `getStaticPaths` to a page, with or without params (e.g. `pages/category/[category].js`), the page doesn't compile anymore on development (it works fine if I build it and run with `NODE_ENV=production`).\r\n\r\nI get the following error: `TypeError: Cannot destructure property 'publicRuntimeConfig' of 'next_config__WEBPACK_IMPORTED_MODULE_7___default(...)(...)' as it is undefined.`, which corresponds to this:\r\n```javascript\r\nimport getConfig from 'next/config';\r\n\r\nconst { publicRuntimeConfig } = getConfig();\r\n```\r\n\r\nAfter reading the [documentation for `next/config`](https://nextjs.org/docs/api-reference/next.config.js/runtime-configuration), I still don't really understand if it should work or not. I've also seen the [env documentation](https://nextjs.org/docs/api-reference/next.config.js/environment-variables) and it seems promising, but it would take a while to migrate everything from `publicRuntimeConfig`.\r\n\r\nAlso, removing `getStaticPaths` and keeping `getStaticProps` works fine (for pages without params obviously, you need `getStaticPaths` for dynamic pages). I don't have any logic inside `getStaticPaths`, it's just a return statement with all the required fields.\r\n\r\nDoes anyone have any idea what could be wrong or if this is a bug? I could look into migrating to env variables, but I'm not sure if they work on client-side (do they?).  \r\nSuggestions appreciated.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n*Edit:*\r\n\r\nSince I've forgotten and it might be useful, here are my system details:\r\n- `next version`: 9.3.2\r\n- `nodejs version`: 13.7.0\r\n- OS: Windows 10 1909 (WSL using Ubuntu 18.04 LTS)\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n*Edit 2:*\r\n\r\nI've just tested with a new next app, it still happens. Here is a Gist that reproduces it: https://gist.github.com/diogotcorreia/<HASH_REDACTED>\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n*Edit 3:*\r\n\r\nThis is expected behaviour: https://github.com/zeit/next.js/issues/12166", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 6, "reactions_total": 14, "reactions_plus": 13, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 1, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "diogotcorreia", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2020-03-30T15:19:59Z", "updated_at": "2022-06-01T12:42:30Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/11493", "classification": "random"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 11498, "title": "isSerializable does not include Date type", "body": "https://github.com/zeit/next.js/blob/master/packages/next/lib/is-serializable-props.ts#L41\r\n\r\nIs it possible that Date as type is missing from this method? I am getting an error when trying to export my site as a static one and when the object contains date values.\r\n\r\nTemporary workaround is to cast the date type as a string", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 26, "reactions_total": 0, "reactions_plus": 0, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "XavierGeerinck", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2020-03-30T16:24:55Z", "updated_at": "2022-12-05T13:12:23Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/11498", "classification": "need-related"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 11500, "title": "GET http://localhost:3000/_next/static/idgeXWAXPu9_DPp3bjsFl/pages/eventos/Il-Divo.js net::ERR_ABORTED 404 (Not Found)", "body": "GET http://localhost:3000/_next/static/idgeXWAXPu9_DPp3bjsFl/pages/eventos/Il-Divo.js net::ERR_ABORTED 404 (Not Found)\r\n\r\nHi I have the next issue that occur in dev, but also occur in production bundle.\r\nAnd also display me also this error in prod environment:\r\n\r\nUncaught (in promise) Error: Error loading script /_next/static/ifPm7_b1UGXrYSoe_o_Oh/pages/eventos/Ill-Divo.js\r\nat HTMLScriptElement.a.onerror (main-68a23d2\u2026.js:1)\r\n\r\nI have Next/Link with the next config\r\n\r\n```\r\nconst url={`/eventos/${event.seo}`}\r\n<Link href={url} as={url}>{event.name}</Link>\r\n```\r\nand I have a custom routing with express\r\n\r\n```\r\n...\r\nconst routes = require('next-routes')\r\nmodule.exports = routes()\r\n.add('index', '/')\r\n.add('event', '/eventos/:seo')\r\n....\r\n```\r\n\r\nmy custom server is\r\n\r\n```\r\n...\r\nconst nextApp = require('next')\r\nconst express = require('express')\r\nconst app = nextApp({\r\n     dev\r\n})\r\nconst handler = routes.getRequestHandler(app)\r\nconst server = express()\r\napp.prepare().then(() => {\r\n       server.use(handler).listen(port, err => {\r\n      if (err) {  \r\n          console.error('Error starting server', err)\r\n       } else {\r\n            /_ eslint-disable no-console _/\r\n           console.log(`Server started on port ${port} at ${new Date()}`)\r\n       }\r\n   })\r\n})\r\n...\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\n![Screen Shot 2020-03-30 at 10 43 45](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/33262684/77938729-633d7900-7273-11ea-932c-65df730342a4.png)\r\n\r\ndependencies\u00b4s version\r\n\r\n\"next\": \"^9.3.1\",\r\n\"next-routes\": \"^1.4.2\",\r\n\"express\": \"^4.17.0\",\r\n\r\nOS: macOS, Windows\r\nBrowser all\r\n\r\nAnyone help me?\r\n", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 0, "reactions_total": 0, "reactions_plus": 0, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "canotech", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2020-03-30T16:48:21Z", "updated_at": "2022-06-26T00:47:37Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/11500", "classification": "random"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 11501, "title": "Custom error page get filename and line number from error", "body": "# Feature request\r\n\r\n## Is your feature request related to a problem? Please describe.\r\n\r\nI'm trying to catch all errors in my website and sent them to slack so i'm aware of all errors. I created an _error.js file and in getInitialProps i'm sending the error to my back-end. It looks like this:\r\n\r\npages/_errors.js\r\n```js\r\nError.getInitialProps = async ({res, err, req}) => {\r\n    axios.post('/api/notifications', {\r\n        notification: 'Front-end error',\r\n        url: req ? req.path : Router.asPath,\r\n        message: err ? err.message : 'Something went wrong',\r\n        status: err && err.statusCode ? err.statusCode : res.statusCode\r\n    })\r\n})\r\n```\r\nNow this works and is great, but most of the time I have no idea were the error comes from. I'm missing information like in which file and line number the error took place.\r\n\r\nIsn't this possible to retrieve this from err?\r\n\r\n## Describe the solution you'd like\r\n\r\nI would like to have more information from the error available like:\r\n\r\n```js\r\nerr.fileName\r\nerr.linenumber\r\n```\r\n", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 1, "reactions_total": 0, "reactions_plus": 0, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "tychovbh", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2020-03-30T20:03:45Z", "updated_at": "2022-06-08T12:13:18Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/11501", "classification": "random"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 11506, "title": "Share data props between static paths", "body": "Hi\r\nI was looking for a possibility to share props between pages in the SSG context. I read this comment: https://github.com/zeit/next.js/issues/10933#issuecomment-598297975 and followed this discussion: https://github.com/zeit/next.js/discussions/11370\r\n\r\nMy request is slightly different: I use headless CMS and the payload for each page consist of a json response similar like this:\r\n```js\r\nexport const getStaticProps = (props) => {\r\nconst {page, settings, staticElements, routes} = await getContentFromStoryblok(props)\r\nreturn {\r\n props:{page,settings,staticElements,routes}\r\n}\r\n}\r\n```\r\nThe only data which is unique for each slug is `page` whilst `settings,staticElements,routes` will not change. \r\nIs there a way to write `settings,staticElements,routes` as static json into the cache and make it available inside of my app component on client render?", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 0, "reactions_total": 0, "reactions_plus": 0, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "dohomi", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2020-03-31T01:14:16Z", "updated_at": "2020-12-01T22:04:54Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/11506", "classification": "need-related"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 11508, "title": "Dev Proxy to external API", "body": "I've been googling for a while now, trying to figure out how to proxy certain URLs to a separate API, not hosted by Next.js.\r\n\r\nMy current attempt was to edit the webpack config, because that's wat some issues in this repo said to do.  So I had the following in my `next.config.js`\r\n\r\n    const { PHASE_DEVELOPMENT_SERVER } = require('next/constants');\r\n  \r\n    module.exports = (phase, { defaultConfig }) => {\r\n        if (phase === PHASE_DEVELOPMENT_SERVER) {\r\n            return {\r\n                /* development only config options here */\r\n                webpack: (webpackConfig) => {\r\n                    const newConfig = { ...webpackConfig };\r\n                    newConfig.devServer = {\r\n                        ...webpackConfig.devServer,\r\n                        proxy: [{\r\n                            context: ['/api', '/admin', '/staticfiles'],\r\n                            target: 'http://localhost:8000',\r\n                        }]\r\n                    };\r\n                    return newConfig;\r\n                },\r\n                cdn: false,\r\n            }\r\n        }\r\n    }\r\n\r\nBut that doesn't work.  When I go to `/api/` on my page, it returns the 404 route.  \r\n\r\nSo what would be the best way to proxy `/api` to `http://localhost:8000` (no rewrite) using the next dev server (`npm run dev` where dev is `next dev`).", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 4, "reactions_total": 0, "reactions_plus": 0, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "cclloyd", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2020-03-31T03:36:15Z", "updated_at": "2022-07-05T13:23:52Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/11508", "classification": "need-related"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 11510, "title": "Is there built-in feature to bundle custom server?", "body": "Is there built-in feature to bundle custom server along with next.js bundle?\r\n\r\nTo decrease size of application image I am going to configure Webpack to bundle custom server,\r\nBut I wonder if I do not have to do it.\r\n\r\nThanks!", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 0, "reactions_total": 1, "reactions_plus": 1, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "ivansky", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2020-03-31T06:23:02Z", "updated_at": "2020-12-01T22:04:55Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/11510", "classification": "random"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 11511, "title": "Cannot suppress \"Module not found: Can't resolve\" warning", "body": "# Bug report\r\n\r\n## Describe the bug\r\nHello everyone,\r\n\r\nin the project I'm working on we require on a file which might exist or not:\r\n\r\n```\r\ntry {\r\n  projectFonts = require('../../config/colors')\r\n} catch (ex) {\r\n  // we dont need a catch handler here as the projectFonts are optional\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis causes a lot of `Module not found: Can't resolve '../../config/colors' in...` warnings on the console.\r\n\r\nI tried to suppress these warnings by adding this line of code to the next.config.js \r\n`config.stats = {warning: false}`:\r\n\r\n```\r\n// imports...\r\n\r\nmodule.exports = withStylus({\r\n  webpack: config => {\r\n    config.plugins = config.plugins || []\r\n    config.stats = {warning: false}\r\n\r\n    config.plugins = [\r\n      ...config.plugins,\r\n\r\n      // Read the .env file\r\n      new Dotenv({\r\n        path: path.join(__dirname, '.env'),\r\n        systemvars: true,\r\n      }),\r\n    ]\r\n\r\n    return config\r\n  },\r\n})\r\n```\r\n## Expected behavior\r\n\r\nI expected, that `config.stats = {warning: false}` will prevent the warning from being displayed (as mentioned here https://github.com/webpack/webpack.js.org/issues/147#issuecomment-253736058)\r\n\r\n\r\n## System information\r\n\r\n- OS: Ubuntu\r\n- Version of Next.js: 9.3.2\r\n\r\n\r\nThanks for your help!\r\n", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 3, "reactions_total": 0, "reactions_plus": 0, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "hagealex", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2020-03-31T07:23:17Z", "updated_at": "2023-07-16T16:59:42Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/11511", "classification": "random"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 11512, "title": "Test coverage in Next.js codebase", "body": "Hi,\r\n\r\nIs there a particular reason why the test coverage is not being measured in the CI pipelines? \r\n\r\nFrom what I can find, Next.js at one point in time did have support for measuring code coverage (#244 and [c56fde89](https://github.com/zeit/next.js/commit/<HASH_REDACTED>)) and also published the results to Coveralls, but this was eventually removed from the repository (#7689). Is there any reason for this?", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 7, "reactions_total": 0, "reactions_plus": 0, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "fabianishere", "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR", "created_at": "2020-03-31T08:46:07Z", "updated_at": "2022-06-05T18:00:25Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/11512", "classification": "need-related"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 11514, "title": "Not Every Import CSS is a global CSS", "body": "Example: i have flatpickr css that only used in particular component.\r\nwhy do i have to put it on global, because on global css its requested on every pages.", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 1, "reactions_total": 2, "reactions_plus": 2, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "rifky-rangkuti", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2020-03-31T09:53:09Z", "updated_at": "2020-12-01T22:04:54Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/11514", "classification": "random"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 11517, "title": "SSG export routing missing .html", "body": "# Bug report\r\n\r\n## Describe the bug\r\n\r\nOn an exported site, the routing works via links however the URLs in browser do not get suffixed with .html and therefore if someone wishes to share a link, it does not work.\r\n\r\n## To Reproduce\r\n\r\nSteps to reproduce the behavior, please provide code snippets or a repository:\r\n\r\n1. Create next site\r\n2. Create /pages/test.js and add basic content. Add `<Link href=\"/test\"><a>Visit test.js</a></Link>` on index.js\r\n3. `next build && next export`\r\n4. Deploy `/out` folder to static website hosting\r\n5. Visit url. Click Visit test.js\r\n6. Page loads\r\n7. Copy URL\r\n8. Goto new tab in browser and paste URL\r\n9. Page not found error (404)\r\n\r\n## Expected behavior\r\n\r\nEither the route in URL should be .html or the route when copied should work when shared.\r\n\r\n## System information\r\n\r\n- OS: any\r\n- Browser (if applies) any\r\n- Version of Next.js: canary\r\n", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 7, "reactions_total": 1, "reactions_plus": 1, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "1jmj", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2020-03-31T11:10:48Z", "updated_at": "2025-01-22T09:02:56Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/11517", "classification": "random"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 11518, "title": "Hybrid feature to SSG and SSR based on the date created", "body": "Hello,\r\nI haven't used the SSG on NextJS yet, but i have read about it and its really cool.\r\nI was wondering what would be the Build time if i had to SSG for ~50k blog posts.\r\nI assume its gonna take ~30 mins based on server configuration...\r\n\r\nBut also, i was wondering if it was possible to SSG recent 100 blog posts and SSR the remaining blog posts. ?", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 2, "reactions_total": 0, "reactions_plus": 0, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "eltonjothi", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2020-03-31T11:14:25Z", "updated_at": "2022-08-23T03:26:36Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/11518", "classification": "random"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 11522, "title": "getStaticProps + getStaticPaths: When updating new article latest content is not fetched", "body": "Hi guys.\r\n\r\nFirst I would like to say how amazing the updates in v9.3. I applied it immediately to my site and the results are blazing fast! However, I got some confusion when I updated content for an existing blog article (/post/[slug] with getStaticProps + getStaticPaths). \r\n\r\nSupposed I added new images and texts in CMS side, how do I make sure those changes get reflected in production? In development (now dev) the changes are instant without me needing to do anything.\r\n\r\nI followed the docs and I hope I didn't miss the instructions. I'd be happy if someone could point ,e in the right direction.\r\n\r\nCheers! ", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 0, "reactions_total": 0, "reactions_plus": 0, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "carthegian", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2020-03-31T13:47:57Z", "updated_at": "2020-12-01T22:04:54Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/11522", "classification": "need-related"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 11525, "title": "Why does renderToHTML with getServerSideProps send response, return null?", "body": "I would like to get the HTML result of a render of page components that use getServerSideProps, but there is a check in `renderToHTMLWithComponnets()` (packages/next/next-server/server/next-server.ts, line 996) that forces the response to be sent immediately instead of being returned.\r\n\r\n```TypeScript\r\n      if (html && isServerProps) {\r\n        sendPayload(res, html, 'html', {\r\n          private: isPreviewMode,\r\n          stateful: true, // GSSP request\r\n        })\r\n        return null\r\n      }\r\n```\r\n\r\nMy hope was to cache the result.\r\n\r\nCan someone help me figure out why this is desirable as designed? It seems to be on purpose, so it feels like I'm using it wrong.", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 2, "reactions_total": 1, "reactions_plus": 1, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "visum", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2020-03-31T15:33:01Z", "updated_at": "2022-10-05T02:05:58Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/11525", "classification": "need-related"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 11530, "title": "NextAuth example works locally but fails on Zeit", "body": "Hey all,\r\n\r\nIn the NextAuth example (https://github.com/iaincollins/next-auth/tree/master/example), the file `pages/auth/index.js` has the following code:\r\n\r\n```js\r\nimport React from 'react'\r\nimport Router from 'next/router'\r\nimport { NextAuth } from 'next-auth/client'\r\nimport Layout from '../../components/layout'\r\n\r\nexport default class extends React.Component {\r\n  \r\n  static async getInitialProps({req}) {\r\n    return {\r\n      session: await NextAuth.init({req}),\r\n      linkedAccounts: await NextAuth.linked({req}),\r\n      providers: await NextAuth.providers({req})\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  render() {\r\n    ...\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis page works perfectly fine when running locally, but unfortunately fails when deployed to Zeit using now.\r\n\r\nIn the deployment, I get the following error:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1161\" alt=\"Screen Shot 2020-03-31 at 12 31 54 PM\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/994646/78070747-53ed2700-736a-11ea-9efb-9819866578c4.png\">\r\n\r\nI tried troubleshooting this to no avail.\r\n\r\nI saw this note in the NextAuth documentation:\r\n\r\n> CSRF, Session and Linked Account endpoints are provided for Single Page Apps.\r\n\r\nBased on this, I had a suspicion that `NextAuth.linked` and `NextAuth.providers` shouldn't be called on the server and should only be called on the client, so I modified the code to only call these functions on the client.\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, this didn't fix the problem. The page still shows a server error when it is loaded on the client.\r\n\r\nWould appreciate any help, and would be great to find out if this is an issue with NextAuth, Next.js, Zeit, or one of my minor modifications.\r\n\r\nThanks!", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 10, "reactions_total": 0, "reactions_plus": 0, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "shea256", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2020-03-31T20:15:42Z", "updated_at": "2022-06-02T06:00:31Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/11530", "classification": "random"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 11531, "title": "Trouble running TakeShape App for the first time", "body": "Hey, \r\nI am relatively new to web development and wanted to start a site with zeit.co and TakeShape. I followed the documentation until the end and thought I did everything correctly, but I can't get the app to run even locally. This is the error message I get: \r\n\"Error serializing `.allPosts` returned from `getStaticProps` in \"/\". Reason: `undefined` cannot be serialized as JSON. Please use `null` or omit this value all together.\"\r\nI can't figure out what that means because I don't yet understand the concept of staticProps. Any help would be much appreciated!", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 2, "reactions_total": 0, "reactions_plus": 0, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "severinschmid", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2020-03-31T20:48:47Z", "updated_at": "2020-12-01T22:04:54Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/11531", "classification": "need-related"}
