{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 11541, "title": "Fauna cookie auth example", "body": "I'm following along with the `with-cookie-auth-fauna` from the examples. I've set up my fauna database, collection, index and server key.\r\n\r\nI've hit a roadblock when trying to login or register a user: I get a 401 unauthorized back from Fauna.\r\n\r\nI'm wondering whether I've set the FAUNA_SECRET_COOKIE wrong? Do I need to change that to something that I get from the fauna dashboard, or just set it to something unique?", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 0, "reactions_total": 0, "reactions_plus": 0, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "bradders", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2020-04-01T05:42:15Z", "updated_at": "2020-12-01T22:04:54Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/11541", "classification": "random"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 11544, "title": "Custom 404 page not picked up?", "body": "https://codesandbox.io/s/nextjs-933-custom-404-page-x6r6f\r\n\r\nWhen you go to /404, then 404.js page is rendered. When you go to /doesnotexist, then the standard Next.js 404 page is rendered.\r\n\r\nI'm not sure what else I'm supposed to do. The documentation (https://nextjs.org/docs/advanced-features/custom-error-page#404-page) says to create `pages/404.js` which is what I did.", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 2, "reactions_total": 0, "reactions_plus": 0, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "wereHamster", "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR", "created_at": "2020-04-01T09:15:12Z", "updated_at": "2022-06-21T15:29:46Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/11544", "classification": "need-related"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 11545, "title": "Custom polyfill only for legacy browsers?", "body": "I'm using custom polyfills as intersection-observer, and I added them in my project following this example:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/zeit/next.js/blob/canary/examples/with-polyfills/next.config.js\r\n\r\nHowever, these polyfills are added also in modern browsers. Is there another way to do it only for legacy browsers? (This example is very old and the things changed so fast in Next.js)", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 4, "reactions_total": 0, "reactions_plus": 0, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "aralroca", "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR", "created_at": "2020-04-01T09:44:06Z", "updated_at": "2022-09-18T16:31:15Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/11545", "classification": "random"}
