{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 11705, "title": "Cant find my site on google", "body": "I created a nextjs site. It has a sitemap all of which I can see in my google console. when i go to site:mysite.com I can see all my pages indexed but when I do a search for my site on google, I cant find it. I have meta keyword and meta descriptions and Ive verified my domain with google. Any help?", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 12, "reactions_total": 0, "reactions_plus": 0, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "webface", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2020-04-06T17:53:52Z", "updated_at": "2025-02-05T09:37:12Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/11705", "classification": "random"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 11713, "title": "Dynamic Routes when using a Reverse Proxy", "body": "I have a new NextJS project that I'd like to point to from a different domain and directory using a reverse proxy. So for instance, maindomain.com/path/site/ will point to the root at whatever.now.sh. And I have dynamic routes setup for all of the content, under page/[id].js. I have configured assetPrefix and used publicRuntimeConfig to get all of the assets loading correctly. The one issue is dynamic routing, as adding the base path prefix to the dynamic routes, while it sort of works, causes a hard page refresh and isn't loading the route via client side correctly.\r\n\r\nMy links are done via onClick like so:\r\nrouter.push(`/?id=${id}`, `${basePath}/page/${id}`, {shallow: true})\r\n\r\ngetStaticPaths looks something like this:\r\n```\r\nexport async function getStaticPaths() {\r\n  const data = await DataLoader.fetch('pages') // returns a content array with unique ids\r\n  const paths = data.map(({id}) => ({params: {id}))\r\n    return {\r\n      paths,\r\n      fallback: false\r\n    }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nindex.js and page/[id].json share most of the same code, with the exception of getStaticPaths\r\n\r\nMy dynamic routes are built using the page/[id].js paradigm and getStaticPaths. Would just using exportPathMap in next.config.js make any bit of difference? What would cause a hard refresh to occur and not a client-side only route change?", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 0, "reactions_total": 0, "reactions_plus": 0, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "tankadesign", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2020-04-06T21:31:24Z", "updated_at": "2022-07-18T09:39:37Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/11713", "classification": "random"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 11718, "title": "How to fetch dynamic data on pre-rendered routes?", "body": "Right now I'm rendering a product page (`/pages/product`) via getStaticProps which contains links (dynamic routes) to product detail pages (`/pages/product/[name]`) for each respective product that I'm pre-rendering using getStaticPaths. As you can imagine a lot of product information (image, name, price, etc.) are static, however, things like stock or status (available, out-of-stock, etc.) are dynamic. What I'm trying to do is fetch this dynamic data via SWR on the pre-rendered route (product detail page), but am encountering the following error: \r\n\r\n**Error: Invalid hook call. Hooks can only be called inside of the body of a function component.**\r\n\r\nIn `/pages/product/[name]`:\r\n```\r\nconst ProductPage = ( { product } ) => {\r\n     const { data } = useSWR('/api/status?_id=' + product._id, fetcher);\r\n     \r\n     return (\r\n          ...\r\n     )\r\n}\r\n\r\nexport async function getStaticPaths() {\r\n     # connect to db\r\n     # fetch all products\r\n     const paths = products.map(product => ({\r\n          params: { name: product.name }\r\n      }));\r\n     \r\n     return { paths, fallback: false };\r\n}\r\n\r\nexport async function getStaticProps({ params }) {\r\n     # connect to db\r\n     # fetch singular product based on name\r\n     return {\r\n          props: { product }\r\n       };\r\n}\r\n\r\nexport default ProductPage;\r\n```\r\n\r\nI'm a bit unclear as to what this error means and if there exists a way to fetch this dynamic data via SWR. I believe the Incremental Static Generation RFC could solve my problems as I can fetch stock and status at build time and revalidate every couple of minutes. However, I was wondering if there was a way to fetch this information in the meantime. Thank you.", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 0, "reactions_total": 0, "reactions_plus": 0, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "visakadivines", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2020-04-07T01:50:45Z", "updated_at": "2022-07-03T21:05:46Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/11718", "classification": "need-related"}
{"repo": "vercel/next.js", "number": 11719, "title": "How can we integrate .mdx files using new SSG functions?", "body": "How can we integrate `.mdx` files using the new SSG functions?\r\n\r\nI've tried using these examples, but there's some glue missing to set up a blog with custom files, gray-matter, etc.:\r\n* http://github.com/timer/blog\r\n* https://github.com/zeit/next.js/tree/canary/examples/with-mdx\r\n\r\nIf we try to replicate a setup like https://github.com/kentcdodds/kentcdodds.com (uses gatsby) are we missing some functions, or am I just missing an example that wires it all up?", "category": "Help", "category_slug": "help", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 7, "reactions_total": 0, "reactions_plus": 0, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "NateRadebaugh", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2020-04-07T02:57:49Z", "updated_at": "2022-07-28T18:47:16Z", "url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/11719", "classification": "random"}
