{"repo": "denoland/deno", "number": 14616, "title": "Persist localStorage wihout --location when upgrading installed scripts?", "body": "The `--location` flag will persist localStorage over script upgrades:\r\n\r\n\r\n```bash\r\n# INSTALL v0.0.1\r\n$ deno install --location=<URL> <SERVER>@0.0.1/test.js\r\n\r\n$ test\r\nlocalStorage is empty\r\n\r\n$ test\r\nlocalStorage has data\r\n\r\n\r\n# UPGRADE to v0.0.2\r\n$ deno install -f --location=<URL> <SERVER>@0.0.2/test.js\r\n\r\n$ test\r\nlocalStorage has data\r\n```\r\n\r\nExample script:\r\n```js\r\n// test.js\r\n#!/usr/bin/env -S deno run\r\nconsole.log(localStorage.getItem('test') || 'localStorge is empty');\r\nlocalStorage.setItem('test', 'localStorage has data');\r\n```\r\n\r\nBut is it possible to persist localStorage ***without*** using the `--location` flag?\r\n\r\nThank you.", "category": "Q&A", "category_slug": "q-a", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 2, "reactions_total": 0, "reactions_plus": 0, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "ekmwest", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2022-05-15T12:29:07Z", "updated_at": "2022-06-10T20:49:36Z", "url": "https://github.com/denoland/deno/discussions/14616", "classification": "random"}
{"repo": "denoland/deno", "number": 14673, "title": "Awesome Deno Organization", "body": "Welcome to Deno!\r\n\ud83e\udd96\ud83e\udd96\ud83e\udd96\ud83e\udd96\ud83e\udd96\ud83e\udd96\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/denorg\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/denosaurs\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/denolib\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/denolibs\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/deno-npm\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/Deno-Sandbox\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/Denoot\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/denoflow\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/deno-front-end\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/astrodon\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/denostack\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/deno-web3\r\n", "category": "General", "category_slug": "general", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 2, "reactions_total": 2, "reactions_plus": 0, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 2, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "sunw31", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2022-05-19T15:14:23Z", "updated_at": "2022-05-20T07:35:33Z", "url": "https://github.com/denoland/deno/discussions/14673", "classification": "random"}
{"repo": "denoland/deno", "number": 14707, "title": "Differences between async and sync functions", "body": "Hi I'm still trying to understand if I got this correctly\r\n\r\n```\r\ntry { Deno.statSync(cacheDir) //sync cause I first need to try stat and see if the file already exists before doing something based on this info\r\n         //file exists let's use the cache\r\n            return cachedVersion(cacheDir)\r\n} catch(err) {\r\n         //file doesn't exist lat's create cache for next requests\r\n           render = renderSomething()\r\n            Deno.writeTextFile(cacheDir, render, {create: true}) //create file in async way since we don't need to use it now\r\n            return render\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nI'm not sure why but the .stat async method works as well, what's really confusing me is the try catch statement instead of a simple if (fileExists(file). But anyway to my logic I need to do that in a sync way since on that it depends the result of the try and catch, while the creation of the cached version can happen in async while the server keeps preparing the response for the client.\r\nAny suggestions to make this more clear?\r\nThanks", "category": "Q&A", "category_slug": "q-a", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 7, "reactions_total": 0, "reactions_plus": 0, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "lordanubi", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2022-05-23T21:45:47Z", "updated_at": "2022-06-27T07:41:58Z", "url": "https://github.com/denoland/deno/discussions/14707", "classification": "random"}
{"repo": "denoland/deno", "number": 14715, "title": "Is there a recommended way to remove temporary directories and files?", "body": "Hi, I was wondering when and how it is sensible to manually remove temporary directories that are only required while a process is running. Initially, I was using the unload event to remove all directories after the process had successfully completed \u2013\r\n\r\n```ts\r\nconst tempPath = await Deno.makeTempDir();\r\n\r\nglobalThis.onunload = (e: Event): void => {\r\n  Deno.remove(tempPath , { recursive: true });\r\n};\r\n```\r\n\r\nHowever, the function is never called and the directory remains when the process terminates due to an exception.  So, for the time being, I'm removing any old directories from previous runs at the start of the process.  Similar to this \u2013 \r\n\r\n```ts\r\nconst tempPath = await Deno.makeTempDir({ prefix: `my-prefix-` });\r\n\r\nfor await (const dirEntry of Deno.readDir(path.resolve(tempPath, `../`))) {\r\n  if (!dirEntry.name.startsWith(`my-prefix-`)) continue;\r\n \r\n  const olderPath = path.resolve(tempPath, `../${dirEntry.name}`);\r\n\r\n  if (tempPath != olderPath) {\r\n    Deno.remove(olderPath, { recursive: true });\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nAre there recommended methods for doing this with Deno? ", "category": "Q&A", "category_slug": "q-a", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 4, "reactions_total": 0, "reactions_plus": 0, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "milotheirself", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2022-05-24T17:52:33Z", "updated_at": "2022-06-11T08:58:20Z", "url": "https://github.com/denoland/deno/discussions/14715", "classification": "need-related"}
{"repo": "denoland/deno", "number": 14736, "title": "improve typescript compilation times with snapshots", "body": "so the typescript repo has an issue discussing speeding up the compiler, I thought I would share that issue here https://github.com/microsoft/TypeScript/issues/25658#issuecomment-1138877141. Especially of note, is that node 18 supports user-land snapshotting https://nodejs.org/en/blog/announcements/v18-release-announce/#build-time-user-land-snapshot-experimental, and the effort appears to be mostly focused on speeding up the compiler using snapshots.\r\n\r\nThis is an interesting feature, and I can imagine use cases outside the tsc compiler, but this seems like the most immediately valuable place to use snapshotting.\r\n\r\nAs far as I know, deno already does some snapshotting of user code to improve startup times. It could be valuable to do the same for the typescript compiler. Please correct me if this is something deno already does \ud83d\ude05 ", "category": "Ideas", "category_slug": "ideas", "state": "open", "state_reason": null, "comments": 2, "reactions_total": 0, "reactions_plus": 0, "reactions_minus": 0, "reactions_laugh": 0, "reactions_hooray": 0, "reactions_confused": 0, "reactions_heart": 0, "reactions_rocket": 0, "reactions_eyes": 0, "author": "andykais", "author_association": "NONE", "created_at": "2022-05-26T19:35:47Z", "updated_at": "2022-06-02T14:24:08Z", "url": "https://github.com/denoland/deno/discussions/14736", "classification": "random"}
